# THIS FILE IS MANAGED BY PUPPET
# Insert rules into DOCKER-USER chain for Docker traffic acceptance
# These rules are typically needed to allow Docker containers to communicate
# and for inbound traffic to reach published ports, especially when
# other firewall rules might interfere or if Docker's own iptables/nftables
# management is not fully robust for custom setups.
# The 'counter' keyword enables packet and byte counters for these rules.

add rule ip filter DOCKER-USER counter accept
add rule ip6 filter DOCKER-USER counter accept
